  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> be two vectors such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>|</mo><mn>3</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>|</mo></math> and the angle between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> is a unit vector, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>|</mo></math> is equal to :&nbsp;</p>"
